  "reason": "1) No prior evidence exists, so the critical uncertainty is whether the task is solvable at all and what the performance floor looks like. 2) config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest viable configuration: a single RNA profile reduced by PCA with no aggregation or fusion. It establishes a clean baseline that isolates the raw predictive signal in the RNA data without confounding from encoder choice, profile multiplicity, or cross-modal fusion. 3) Under a limited budget, starting with the cheapest, most interpretable experiment is the most efficient first step: it is fast to train, provides a reference point against which every added complexity (better encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion strategy) can be measured, and avoids prematurely investing in complex multimodal or learned-encoder configurations whose marginal value over a simple PCA baseline is still unknown."
